# Shared-file ownership, machine-readable.
#
# This file does NOT introduce a new ownership model. `docs/28-parallel-workstreams.md` §"Owns
# (write access)" has been the authority since Wave 0, and this is that table in a form a script
# can check. Where the two could disagree, docs/28 wins and this file is wrong — say so rather
# than editing around it.
#
# Phase 2 shows why the machine-readable form was needed: the rule already existed and was
# breached anyway. `make check-collisions` lists the breaches. Nothing was enforcing it.
#
# Format:  <glob>  <owner>
#   - Later lines win, so a specific path can carve itself out of a broad rule.
#   - `**` spans directories; a bare path matches exactly.
#   - owner is a stream letter (A/B/C/D), SHARED for coordinate-before-editing, ANY for free.
#
# Checked by `scripts/check_ownership.py`; protocol in `docs/35-integration-protocol.md`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- default
# Unclaimed paths are SHARED, not free. An unowned file is how Phase 2's conflicts started:
# everyone assumed nobody minded. `make check-owners-audit` keeps this list intentional.
*                                               SHARED

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- A · Core & API
backend/app/orchestrator/**                     A
backend/app/events/**                           A
backend/app/api/**                              A
backend/app/agents/**                           A
backend/app/llm/**                              A
backend/app/observability/**                    A
backend/app/schemas/**                          A
backend/app/config.py                           A
backend/app/main.py                             A
backend/app/cli.py                              A
backend/app/errors.py                           A
docker-compose.yml                              A
Makefile                                        A
.kiro/**                                        A
docs/**                                         A
scripts/**                                      A

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- B · Assurance & Policy
backend/app/assurance/**                        B
backend/app/policy/**                           B
policy_packs/**                                 B
config/**                                       B

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- C · Data, Providers & Services
backend/app/models/**                           C
backend/app/db/**                               C
backend/app/providers/**                        C
backend/app/services/**                         C
backend/app/memory/**                           C
backend/migrations/**                           C
data/**                                         C
# Contractual: A's endpoints must stay byte-compatible with these and D renders them directly.
fixtures/**                                     C

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- D · Frontend
frontend/**                                     D

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build/runtime plumbing
# Not in docs/28's table because it predates it. Assigned to the stream that runs it: the backend
# image and its migration config belong with the backend's owner of startup, which is A.
backend/Dockerfile                              A
backend/.dockerignore                           A
backend/alembic.ini                             A
backend/pyproject.toml                          A
backend/uv.lock                                 A
backend/.python-version                         A

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- tests follow their code
# docs/28 assigns tests with the code they cover, so the owner of the code owns the test.
backend/tests/**                                SHARED
backend/tests/unit/assurance/**                 B
backend/tests/unit/policy/**                    B
backend/tests/unit/services/**                  C
backend/tests/unit/db/**                        C
backend/tests/unit/orchestrator/**              A
backend/tests/contract/**                       A
backend/tests/e2e/**                            A

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- SHARED
# Team artefacts. A holds the pen for `docs/` above, but the CONTENT of these is agreed by the
# team, so a unilateral edit is a protocol breach even from the nominal owner.
docs/DECISIONS.md                               SHARED
docs/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md                          SHARED
docs/28-parallel-workstreams.md                 SHARED
# Cross-cutting invariant guards. SHARED deliberately: they exist to constrain every stream, so
# no stream may relax or delete one alone. docs/28 already calls this out for
# `test_no_llm_in_services.py`, which C explicitly may not remove.
backend/tests/unit/test_state_machine.py        SHARED
backend/tests/unit/test_no_llm_in_services.py   SHARED
backend/tests/unit/test_contracts.py            SHARED
backend/tests/unit/test_config_fail_closed.py   SHARED
backend/tests/unit/test_crosswind.py            SHARED
docs/35-integration-protocol.md                 SHARED
OWNERS                                          SHARED
README.md                                       SHARED
.env.example                                    SHARED
.gitignore                                      SHARED
